      bearCase: "The proliferation of specific bans and regulations, such as California\'s memecoin law, could lead to a fragmented and overly restrictive global regulatory landscape, stifling innovation and market access. Persistent security vulnerabilities, exemplified by the Zano exploit and rollback, underscore inherent risks in decentralized protocols, potentially eroding investor confidence and causing significant financial losses. The philosophical debate over blockchain immutability versus necessary interventions could also create governance crises.",
